    "slug": "autodesk-inventor",
    "displayName": "Inventor",
    "intro": "Inventor is Autodesk's professional tool for 3D mechanical design. Engineers model parts, assemble them, check how they behave and produce the drawings a workshop needs. The catalogue describes it as product design and engineering tools for 3D mechanical design, simulation, visualisation and documentation.\n\nIn India it is bought by machine builders, special-purpose machine and tooling makers, sheet-metal and fabrication shops, engineering consultancies and the design departments of manufacturers. The annual commitment is priced at {{price:autodesk-inventor}} excluding GST, or {{gst:autodesk-inventor}} with 18% GST, per named user, billed yearly.\n\nThis page explains what you are buying, how it compares with Fusion, and how licensing works, so the Inventor price in India makes sense against your actual workflow.",
    "included": "Our catalogue entry for Inventor is brief, so here is what we can say with confidence, and where we will confirm details for you:\n\n- 3D mechanical design for parts and assemblies\n- Simulation to test designs before they are built\n- Visualisation for presenting designs\n- Documentation, meaning the drawings and manufacturing information that go to the shop floor\n\nThe exact module list varies by release and by how Autodesk packages the product. If you need a specific capability, such as sheet metal, frame design, or a particular simulation type, tell us when you [request a quotation](/enquiry) and we will confirm that it is part of the subscription rather than an assumption.\n\nInventor is also one of the products inside the [Product Design & Manufacturing Collection](/products/autodesk-product-design-manufacturing-collection), which adds other tools for teams that use more than one.",
