      "verdict": "Choose Inventor alone if an engineer does mechanical design and nothing else. A single seat is simple to administer and easy to reassign.\n\nChoose the collection if a person needs Inventor with another tool in the list, whether that is Fusion for generative work, Nastran for analysis, or Vault Basic and Factory Design Utilities for data and layout. Count the products opened per person during the year, not the ones installed.\n\nA sensible mixed estate gives collection seats to senior engineers who span tools, standalone seats to specialists, and Flex to reviewers."
